ext:p>Plot A is a <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://example.invalid/tidal/plot-a">documented shoreline site</text:a>.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="CustomOutline3" text:outline-level="3">Custom Outline Level Three</text:h><text:p>This heading uses a custom style name and an explicit outline level.</text:p><text:h text:outline-level="2">Field Team</text:h><text:p>Members record salinity, shade, and plant cover. This synthetic observation explains how notes move from the first column to the second during a long field report.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 01: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 02: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 03: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 04: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 05: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 06: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 07: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 08: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 09: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 10: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-order marker 11: east marsh samples are logged before west marsh samples in this invented field exercise.</text:p><text:p>Reading-